  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metformin remains the standard first-line medication for type 2 diabetes, but American Diabetes Association guidelines now recommend choosing SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists early based on specific organ protection and health goals rather than blood sugar control alone.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "American Diabetes Association guidelines now recommend choosing SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists early based on specific organ protection and health goals rather than blood sugar control alone"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How They Work and Compare"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "SGLT2 inhibitors (such as Jardiance) are daily oral pills that block sugar reabsorption in the kidneys."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "GLP-1 receptor agonists (such as Ozempic) are usually weekly or daily injections that mimic natural gut hormones to boost insulin and slow digestion."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Blood Sugar & Weight: GLP-1 agonists generally lower HbA1c more (up to 1.5%\u20132%) and produce greater weight loss (4 to 6 kg) compared to SGLT2 inhibitors (A1c reduction up to 1%; weight loss 1 to 3 kg)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "When to Choose SGLT2 Inhibitors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Heart Failure: Highly recommended if you have heart failure, as they reduce hospital stays and death."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Kidney Disease: Preferred for chronic kidney disease to slow down kidney damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Convenience: Taken as a once-daily pill instead of an injection."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "When to Choose GLP-1 Agonists"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Weight Loss: Best choice if significant weight loss or obesity management is a primary goal."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cardiovascular Risk: Preferred to lower the risk of major events like strokes and heart attacks (atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Greater A1c Reduction: Better option when blood sugar is high and needs a stronger drop."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Side Effects"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "SGLT2 inhibitors: Higher risk of urinary tract and genital fungal infections due to sugar passing in the urine."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "GLP-1 agonists: Common stomach issues like nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and constipation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Do you have any other conditions like heart disease, heart failure, or kidney disease?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is weight loss a top priority for you?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you prefer a pill or an injection ?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you discuss these details with your doctor."
      }
    ],
